=== PARITY (vs web OnboardingGate.tsx) ===
  Web source (64 lines) is a NON-VISUAL first-run redirect guard: it reads useOnboardingStatus
  (tesla_connected + vehicle_count + data_flowing + is_complete), useOnboardingSkip (isSkipped),
  useLocation (pathname) and useNavigate, then runs one effect:
      if (isLoading || isError || !data) return;   // hold — never trap the user
      if (data.is_complete) return;                 // pass
      if (isSkipped) return;                        // pass
      if (isAllowed(location.pathname)) return;     // pass
      navigate('/onboarding', { replace: true });   // redirect
  with ALLOW_PREFIXES = ['/onboarding','/tesla-account','/settings','/s/','/watch','/login'] and a
  prefix rule (trailing-slash => startsWith; else exact OR child). It `return null`s and only
  triggers navigation.

  Data sources -> bound through a push-based OnboardingGateSource seam (P1/S8): the app joins the
    shared onboarding-status holder (useOnboardingStatus) + the skip store (useOnboardingSkip) +
    the router's current path (useLocation) into OnboardingGateUpdate(feed, isSkipped, path,
    connection, updatedAt). The view performs NO networking (structurally enforced: the view reads
    only OnboardingGateModel; the model reads only the source).
  Logic -> GateEvaluator is a byte-faithful port of the effect: hold(loading/error/noData) ->
    pass(complete) -> pass(skipped) -> pass(allowListed) -> redirect("/onboarding"), in the web
    branch order. OnboardingAllowList.isAllowed reproduces the trailing-slash/exact/child rule
    verbatim. The redirect is driven through a navigator seam (useNavigate); the model fires it
    ONCE per entry into the redirect verdict (web effect re-runs only when a dep changes the
    outcome) and re-fires after the verdict leaves+re-enters redirect — executed-tested [4].
  Composition -> the web guard is invisible; the prompt requires a real surface with every state
    (no blank box). Native renders a setup-gate card: header (sparkles + title + subtitle +
    freshness chip), a verdict card (complete / continue / redirect with a "Go to setup" CTA), and
    the three onboarding anchors (the status feed's data) as a checklist with an "x of 3" progress.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty/!data (friendly "Setup status
    unavailable" + retry; gate holds) · error/isError (QueryError-equiv + retry; gate holds, never
    trapping — web pessimistic-but-non-redirecting branch) · content[ pass.complete / pass.skipped /
    pass.allowListed / redirect ] · with a live/stale/offline freshness overlay (chip + banner over
    the cached verdict). Each has a #if DEBUG preview.
  i18n -> the web guard has NO t() calls (renders null); every native string the surface introduces
    resolves through the P1/S10 facade (table "OnboardingGate"); 26/26 keys referenced in code are
    PRESENT in OnboardingGate.strings, each English fallback identical to the in-code default. No
    English literals in native code.
  a11y -> the panel is accessibilityElement(.contain) with a composed label; the verdict card +
    notices are .combine; each anchor row carries "name, completed/pending"; the retry + CTA pill
    buttons have accessibilityLabel + .isButton; Dynamic Type via Font.TS tokens; Reduce Motion
    gates the phase transition. Label content is unit-tested via OnboardingGateAccessibility.
  Telemetry -> OnboardingGateModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"OnboardingGate") once ->
    bridges shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy [4].
  Tokens/components -> renders over the REAL apps/apple design system (Color.TS / Font.TS /
    TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion / TSSkeleton); compiled against it in [1]/[1b]. No web Tailwind
    classes ported. Recharts->none / Leaflet->none.

